---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: "/quiz/"
pageId: "later-quiz"
title: "The Quiz"
description: "Quick questions on prices, rent and wealth in the United States: pick an answer, then see the sourced figure."
shareText: "How well do you know the cost of living? Take the Uncost quiz."
---
{#- The cost-of-living quiz (records/changes/CHG-019). Repo-authored since
    CHG-019: tools/gen_static_pages.py no longer writes this file from the
    export's placeholder. pageId stays "later-quiz" because sections.css styles
    the page by it.

    Multiple choice (CHG-019 v2, 2026-11-08). _data/quiz.js holds the ten
    questions and makes every choice from sources/register.csv through
    _data/register.js; the answers render through partials/figure.njk inside
    their data-source. No figure is typed here, in js/quiz.js or in the copy.
    A question that states a number renders inside its row's data-source, and
    _data/quiz.js fails the build if that number is not in the row's caption
    or receipt.

    The choices are listed here as plain text (data-quiz-choice), hidden: the
    content audit's form-rendered rule allows no form control in the built
    page, so js/quiz.js builds each radio group from them at runtime. The wrong
    choices are not register figures; scripts/audit_website.py exempts
    data-quiz-choice text on this page only (CHG-019; CANVAS-SYNC 191).

    Without JavaScript this is the page: the ten questions with their sourced
    answers as a plain list, then the end block; no choices show. js/quiz.js
    turns it into one question at a time. It stores nothing in the browser.
    With the anonymous score tally off (the default), it makes no network
    call. With it on (features.quizStatsOpen), it sends one score at the end
    screen and shows the average (functions/api/quiz/, CHG-019). -#}
{% import "partials/figure.njk" as fig %}
{% import "partials/social-icons.njk" as socialIcon %}
{% set shareUrl = site.origin + page.url %}
{% set shareLine = shareText + " " + shareUrl %}
<!-- SECTION: quiz — title -->
<div class="titleband" data-screen-label="Quiz — title"><h1>The <span class="u-1">Quiz</span></h1></div>
<!-- SECTION: quiz — intro -->
<div class="introband" data-screen-label="Quiz — intro">
  {#- No defer, and before the intro's lines and the questions: js/quiz-early.js
      runs before the parser reaches them, so a slow js/quiz.js (deferred) never
      lets an answer show first, and a build with the score tally on never shows
      a reader with JavaScript the no-JS line. It sits inside a band so the
      bands stay adjacent (.titleband + .introband + .sys). It marks <html> with
      .quiz-js, which integration.css item 150 reads; js/quiz.js removes the mark
      once it has set its own state. The layout has no per-page <head> slot. #}
  <script src="/js/quiz-early.js"></script>
  <h2>Test your knowledge on the <span class="u-1">cost of living</span>.</h2>
  <p>{{ quiz.total }} quick questions on prices, rent and wealth in the United States. Pick an answer, then see the sourced figure.</p>
  {#- With the anonymous score tally on (features.quizStatsOpen; CHG-019), a
      reader with JavaScript sends their score at the end screen, so they read
      the tally line. A reader without JavaScript sends nothing, so they keep
      "Your answers stay in this browser.", which stays true for them. #}
  <p data-quiz-local-note{% if features.quizStatsOpen %} data-quiz-swap{% endif %}>Your answers stay in this browser.</p>
{% if features.quizStatsOpen %}
  <p data-quiz-tally-note hidden>We keep an anonymous tally of scores, with no name, email or IP address, so you can see how you did compared with the average.</p>
{% endif %}
</div>
<div class="sys" data-quiz data-quiz-url="{{ site.origin }}{{ page.url }}" data-quiz-text="{{ shareText }}" data-quiz-version="{{ quiz.version }}"{% if features.quizStatsOpen %} data-quiz-stats{% endif %}>
  <!-- SECTION: quiz — questions -->
  <ol class="quiz-list" data-quiz-list>
{% for q in quiz.questions %}
    <li class="card quiz-q" data-quiz-q data-quiz-kind="{{ q.kind }}" data-screen-label="Quiz — question {{ q.n }}">
      <div class="cap"><p class="quiz-cap">Question {{ q.n }} of {{ quiz.total }}</p></div>
      <div class="bd">
        <div class="eq">{{ q.topic }}</div>
        <h2 id="qz-{{ q.n }}-h" tabindex="-1"{% if q.sourceId %} data-source="{{ q.sourceId }}"{% endif %}>{{ q.question }}</h2>
        <div class="quiz-guess" data-quiz-guess data-quiz-n="{{ q.n }}" data-quiz-record="{{ q.recordText }}" hidden>
          <ul class="quiz-source-list" data-quiz-choices>
{% for c in q.choices %}
            <li data-quiz-choice{% if c.correct %} data-quiz-correct{% endif %}>{{ c.text }}</li>
{% endfor %}
          </ul>
          <div class="actions"><button type="button" class="u-btn u-btn--primary" data-quiz-check disabled>Check my answer</button></div>
        </div>
        {#- The reveal has no heading (founder, 2026-11-08): with JavaScript,
            focus moves to the verdict line ("Correct!" or "Not quite.");
            without it, "The answer: …" leads straight into the figure card,
            which carries the source, period and region. #}
        <div class="quiz-reveal" data-quiz-reveal>
          <p class="quiz-verdict" id="qz-{{ q.n }}-v" tabindex="-1" data-quiz-verdict hidden></p>
          <p class="quiz-answer" data-quiz-nojs data-source="{{ q.row.source_id }}">The answer: {{ q.recordText }}.</p>
          <div class="cards">
      {{ fig.card(q.row) }}
          </div>
{% if q.others.length %}
          <ul class="quiz-others">
{% for r in q.others %}
            <li>{{ fig.line(r) }}</li>
{% endfor %}
          </ul>
{% endif %}
          <div class="actions" data-quiz-next-wrap hidden><button type="button" class="u-btn u-btn--ink" data-quiz-next>Next question</button></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </li>
{% endfor %}
  </ol>
  <!-- SECTION: quiz — end -->
  <div class="card quiz-end" data-quiz-end data-screen-label="Quiz — end">
    <div class="cap"><p class="quiz-cap">Your results</p></div>
    <div class="bd">
      <h2 id="qz-end-h" tabindex="-1">Your answers</h2>
      <p class="quiz-nojs" data-quiz-nojs>Each answer is above, with its source. With JavaScript on, you can pick an answer first and compare.</p>
      {#- One block: the score, then (in a build with the tally on, from 30
          scores) the average and how this reader compares, or "Not enough
          players yet to show an average." js/quiz.js fills both. #}
      <p class="quiz-score" data-quiz-score hidden>You got <span data-quiz-score-n></span> out of {{ quiz.total }} right.<span data-quiz-average hidden></span></p>
      <table class="vhist quiz-sum" data-quiz-summary hidden>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Question</th><th scope="col">Your answer</th><th scope="col">Correct answer</th><th scope="col">Result</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
{% for q in quiz.questions %}
          <tr data-quiz-sum-row><th scope="row">{{ q.topic }}</th><td data-label="Your answer" data-quiz-sum-answer></td><td data-label="Correct answer" data-source="{{ q.row.source_id }}">{{ q.summaryText }}</td><td data-label="Result" data-quiz-sum-right></td></tr>
{% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      {#- No updates form here (founder, 2026-11-08): the site footer, directly
          below, has the same one. Four equal buttons, two by two (one column
          on narrow phones, same order). The Share button needs JavaScript, so
          it stays hidden without it; the share links below show instead. #}
      <p class="quiz-close">Cost of living pressures keep rising. Help the cause, or learn more:</p>
      <div class="quiz-go">
        <button type="button" class="u-btn u-btn--ink" data-quiz-share aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="qz-share" hidden>Share this quiz</button>
        <a href="/pledge/" class="u-btn u-btn--primary">Sign the Pledge</a>
        <a href="/case/" class="u-btn u-btn--ghost">Read The Case</a>
        <a href="/sectors/" class="u-btn u-btn--ghost">Explore the sectors</a>
      </div>
      {#- The share panel (the founder's follow-ups, 2026-11-08). Plain links to
          each network's own share page, opening in a new tab, with the quiz's
          address and shareText (front matter): never the reader's score or
          answers, and no script, widget or request from any network, so the
          CSP is unchanged. scripts/audit_website.py allows each host only as
          a link (ALLOWED_NAV_HOSTS) and fails any address on the host of a
          social account that chrome.json hides, so Reddit's link is built
          only while its account is shown. With JavaScript, js/quiz.js hides
          the panel until "Share this quiz" opens it (Escape closes it) and
          shows "Copy link"; without it, the links are a plain row. #}
      <div class="quiz-share-panel" id="qz-share" data-quiz-share-panel role="group" aria-labelledby="qz-share-cap">
        <p class="quiz-share-cap" id="qz-share-cap">Share this quiz</p>
        <ul class="quiz-share-list">
          <li><a class="quiz-share-link" href="https://x.com/intent/tweet?text={{ shareText | urlencode }}&amp;url={{ shareUrl | urlencode }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Share on X">{{ socialIcon.glyph("X") }}</a></li>
          <li><a class="quiz-share-link" href="https://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u={{ shareUrl | urlencode }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Share on Facebook">{{ socialIcon.glyph("Facebook") }}</a></li>
          <li><a class="quiz-share-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url={{ shareUrl | urlencode }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Share on LinkedIn">{{ socialIcon.glyph("LinkedIn") }}</a></li>
          <li><a class="quiz-share-link" href="https://bsky.app/intent/compose?text={{ shareLine | urlencode }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Share on Bluesky">{{ socialIcon.glyph("Bluesky") }}</a></li>
{% for s in chrome.social %}{% if s.label == "Reddit" and s.show %}          <li><a class="quiz-share-link" href="https://www.reddit.com/submit?url={{ shareUrl | urlencode }}&amp;title={{ shareText | urlencode }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Share on Reddit">{{ socialIcon.glyph("Reddit") }}</a></li>
{% endif %}{% endfor %}
          <li><a class="quiz-share-link" href="https://wa.me/?text={{ shareLine | urlencode }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Share on WhatsApp">{{ socialIcon.glyph("WhatsApp") }}</a></li>
          <li><a class="quiz-share-link" href="mailto:?subject={{ "The Uncost quiz" | urlencode }}&amp;body={{ shareLine | urlencode }}" aria-label="Share by email">{{ socialIcon.glyph("Email") }}</a></li>
          <li data-quiz-copy-wrap hidden><button type="button" class="quiz-share-link" data-quiz-copy aria-label="Copy link"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="2.5" y="12" width="13" height="6" rx="3" transform="rotate(-45 9 15)"></rect><rect x="8.5" y="6" width="13" height="6" rx="3" transform="rotate(-45 15 9)"></rect></svg></button></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <p class="quiz-note" data-quiz-share-note role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="skip-link" data-quiz-live aria-live="polite"></p>
</div>
<script src="/js/quiz.js" defer></script>
